  "id": "Compound::DB00363 - Gene::1576",
  "verbalization": "Clozapine is implicated in the interaction with Cyp2c9, which is a key enzyme involved in the oxidation of various substrates, including quinones and other compounds. This interaction is supported by multiple paths, all of which indicate that Clozapine binds to Cyp2c9 and that this binding leads to its participation in oxidoreductive activities. These activities are then linked to Cyp3a4, suggesting a potential mechanism by which Clozapine influences the activity of Cyp3a4. The evidence suggests that Clozapine may modulate Cyp3a4 through its interaction with Cyp2c9, potentially affecting the metabolic processing of substrates. The recurring theme of oxidoreductive activity and the involvement of Cyp3a4 in this process highlights a possible dependency on Cyp2c9 as a mediator. The integration of these pathways underscores the role of Cyp2c9 in linking Clozapine to Cyp3a4, offering a plausible mechanism for the observed relationship.",
